      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In 1975 Bronx, you'd find a predominantly African American and Latino population. The streets would be filled with Puerto Rican and Dominican gangs, like the Boogie Down Bronx's infamous gang wars. You'd see African American men in dashikis and Afros, likely working at local bodegas or hanging out in the parks. The Puerto Rican women would be working as maids or in the local factories, while the Latino kids would be playing stickball in the streets. Don't forget the Italian-American families, who'd be the quiet, respectable ones on the block.",
